# In a loop, `x instanceof Dog` is decided from shapes, after a guard on the conditions that the class itself must keep. One of them is that it has no Symbol.hasInstance of its own.
# Out of the compiler's sight, Dog gets one that returns true for everything.
# Fault injection, testing=SkipClassGuards: that guard is not built.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) the result is also checked against a lookup that can give up.
# From the tested class up its own prototype chain, the first own property under Symbol.hasInstance must be the engine's own, by identity and as a data property. Otherwise the process crashes.
# The lookup runs no code.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
